{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Imagine throwing a ball vertically upwards. Immediately after release, the ball has kinetic energy. As it rises, gravity does negative work on the ball: the ball's kinetic energy store decreases and its gravitational potential energy store increases. At its highest point, its speed is momentarily zero, so its kinetic energy is zero. As it falls, its gravitational potential energy store decreases while its kinetic energy increases. If air resistance is negligible, the sum of these two stores remains constant. In reality, some energy is transferred to the internal energy stores of the air and ball because of air resistance.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 41.568, "words": [["Imagine", 0.102083], ["throwing", 0.648958], ["a", 0.935416], ["ball", 1.091666], ["vertically", 1.326041], ["upwards.", 1.820833], ["Immediately", 3.359375], ["after", 3.958333], ["release,", 4.296875], ["the", 4.987], ["ball", 5.14325], ["has", 5.338541], ["kinetic", 5.598958], ["energy.", 6.067708], ["As", 7.473958], ["it", 7.708333], ["rises,", 7.890625], ["gravity", 8.697916], ["does", 9.140625], ["negative", 9.348958], ["work", 9.83075], ["on", 10.104166], ["the", 10.247416], ["ball:", 10.403666], ["the", 10.9245], ["ball's", 11.08075], ["kinetic", 11.367208], ["energy", 11.809916], ["store", 12.213541], ["decreases", 12.460958], ["and", 12.95575], ["its", 13.098958], ["gravitational", 13.320333], ["potential", 14.036458], ["energy", 14.596375], ["store", 15.013041], ["increases.", 15.273458], ["At", 16.914083], ["its", 17.135416], ["highest", 17.317708], ["point,", 17.734375], ["its", 18.333333], ["speed", 18.515625], ["is", 18.776041], ["momentarily", 18.945333], ["zero,", 19.53125], ["so", 20.104166], ["its", 20.273458], ["kinetic", 20.46875], ["energy", 20.950541], ["is", 21.380208], ["zero.", 21.497416], ["As", 22.786458], ["it", 23.020833], ["falls,", 23.177083], ["its", 23.854166], ["gravitational", 24